  "texts": {
    "preamble": "K.I.Ibrahim vs The Food Inspector on 8 February, 2016 Author: B.Sudheendra Kumar Bench: B.Sudheendra Kumar In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present: The Honourable Mr. Justice B.Sudheendra Kumar Monday, The 8Th Day Of February 2016/19Th Magha, 1937 Crl.Rev.Pet.No. 1591 of 2010 ( ) --------------------------------- Cra 347/2006 of Ii Addl. Sessions Court, Palakkad St 3087/2001 of J.M.F.C., Pattambi Revision Petitioner(S)/Appellant/Accused: ---------------------------------------- K.I.Ibrahim, S/O.Late Saidalavi, Kooriyatt Thodi House, Mele Pattambi, Pattambi Post Palakkad District. By Advs.Sri.P.Vijaya Bhanu Sri.M.Revikrishnan Respondent(S)/Respondents/Complainant & State: ---------------------------------------------- 1. The Food Inspector, Pattambi Circle, Pattambi. 2. State Of Kerala, Represented By Public Prosecutor High Court Of Kerala, Ernakulam. R By Public Prosecutor Sri.V.S.Sreejith This Criminal Revision Petition Having Been Finally Heard On 08-02-2016, The Court On The Same Day Passed The Following: K.I.Ibrahim vs The Food Inspector on 8 February, 2016 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/128246312/ 1 Scl. B. Sudheendra Kumar, J. ------------------------------------- Crl.R.P.No. 1591 of 2010 -------------------------------------- Dated this the 8th day of February, 2016",
    "facts": "The prosecution allegation can be briefly stated thus:- On 12.11.2001 at about 12 p.m., PW2, the Food Inspector purchased three packets of tamarind, each packet contained 500 gram each, from the accused. It is alleged that the revision petitioner sold the food time without having a valid PFA licence. 4. Before the trial Court, PW1 to PW3 were examined and Exts.P1 to P11 were marked for the prosecution. No evidence was adduced on the side of the revision petitioner.",
